 "sq": [
  {
   "q": "\\(\\text{Find complete integral of } p^2 + q^2 = 4\\)",
   "answer": [
    "Upto the step",
    "Marks",
    "\\(\\text{Let } p=a, q=b \\text{ with } a^2+b^2=4\\)",
    "(1 Mark)",
    "\\(\\text{Then } b=\\sqrt{4-a^2}\\)",
    "(1 Mark)",
    "\\(\\text{Substitute in } dz=p dx+q dy: z=ax+\\sqrt{4-a^2}y+c\\)",
    "(2 Mark)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "q": "",
   "answer": []
  }
 ],
 "lq": [
  {
   "q": "\\(\\text{Find the singular solution of $z=px+qy+\\sqrt{p^2+q^2+1}$.}\\)",
   "answer": [
    "\\(\\text{Therefore, the complete integral is:}\\)",
    "$z=ax+by+\\sqrt{a^2+b^2+1}-----------(2)$",
    "To find the singular integral \\(\\dfrac{\\partial z}{\\partial a}=0\\implies x=-\\dfrac{a}{\\sqrt{a^2+b^2+1}}--------(3)\\) ,",
    "\\(\\dfrac{\\partial z}{\\partial b}=0\\implies y=-\\dfrac{b}{\\sqrt{a^2+b^2+1}}--------(4)\\) .",
    "\\(\\left(3\\right)^2 + \\left(4\\right)^2 \\Rightarrow x^2+y^2=\\dfrac{a^2}{a^2+b^2+1}+\\dfrac{b^2}{a^2+b^2+1}=\\dfrac{a^2+b^2}{a^2+b^2+1} \\)",
    "Subracting from 1 both sides, we get,",
    "\\(1-x^2-y^2=\\dfrac{1}{a^2+b^2+1}\\)",
    "\\(\\Rightarrow 1+a^2+b^2 = \\dfrac{1}{1-x^2-y^2}\\)",
    "\\(\\therefore \\quad \\sqrt{1+a^2+b^2}=\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{1-x^2-y^2}}\\dots(5)\\)",
    "From (3), \\(a=\\dfrac{-x}{\\sqrt{1-x^2-y^2}}\\dots(6)\\)",
    "and from (4), \\(b=\\dfrac{-y}{\\sqrt{1-x^2-y^2}}\\dots(7)\\)",
    "Substituting (5),(6) and (7) in equation (2) , we get",
    "\\(x^2+y^2+z^2 =1 \\qquad \\text{ which is the singular solution.}\\)"
   ]
  }
 ]
